{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-13770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "c01515fc00562e5e50184150fe5e9cf36bab5bc527378c28178084c47e6ee94b"} {"question" "q-13770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries below the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is an upper triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not a lower triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element above the diagonal: ${a}_{12}=1\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "c01515fc00562e5e50184150fe5e9cf36bab5bc527378c28178084c47e6ee94b"} {"question" "q-13770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e19286e95f853a52e485f58892f46cde64ab59c39f32da645ff03f5e3084e006"} {"question" "q-13770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "c01515fc00562e5e50184150fe5e9cf36bab5bc527378c28178084c47e6ee94b"} {"question" "q-13770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Diagonal matrix"] ["text" "Identity matrix"] ["text" "Lower triangular matrix"] ["text" "Other"] ["text" "Upper triangula