6/state.json" "file_sha256" "c01515fc00562e5e50184150fe5e9cf36bab5bc527378c28178084c47e6ee94b"} {"question" "q-13782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "c01515fc00562e5e50184150fe5e9cf36bab5bc527378c28178084c47e6ee94b"} {"question" "q-13782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: ${a}_{21}=2\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "c01515fc00562e5e50184150fe5e9cf36bab5bc527378c28178084c47e6ee94b"} {"question" "q-13782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e19286e95f853a52e485f58892f46cde64ab59c39f32da645ff03f5e3084e006"} {"question" "q-13782" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "c01515fc00562e5e50184150fe5e9cf36bab5bc527378c28178084c47e6ee94b"} {"question" "q-13782" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Diagonal matrix"] ["text" "Identity matrix"] ["text" "Lower triangular matrix"] ["text" "Other"] ["text" "Upper triangular matrix"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "c01515fc00562e5e50184150fe5e9cf36bab5bc527378c28178084c47e6ee94b"} {"question" "q-13782" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "Lower triangular matrix"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "c01515fc00562e5e50184150fe5e9cf36bab5bc527378c28178084c47e6ee94b"} {"question" "q-13760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "c01515fc00562e5e50184150fe5e9cf36bab5bc527378c28178084c47e6ee94b"} {"question" "q-13760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $B$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "c01515fc00562e5e50184150fe5e9cf36bab5bc527378c28178084c47e6ee94b"} {"question" "q-13760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e19286e95f853a52e485f58892f46cde64ab59c39f32da645ff03f5e3084e006"} {"question" "q-13760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "c01515fc00562e5e50184150fe5e9cf36bab5bc527378c28178084c47e6ee94b"} {"question" "q-13760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "c01515fc00562e5e50184150fe5e9cf36bab5bc527378c28178084c47e6ee94b"} {"question" "q-13760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "c01515fc00562e5e50184150fe5e9cf36bab5bc527378c28178084c47e6ee94b"} {"question" "q-126353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "c01515fc00562e5e50184150fe5e9cf36bab5bc527378c28178084c47e6ee94b"} {"question" "q-126353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $B$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "c01515fc00562e5e50184150fe5e9cf36bab5bc527378c28178084c47e6ee94b"} {"question" "q-126353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e19286e95f853a52e485f58892f46cde64ab59c39f32da645ff03f5e3084e006"} {"question" "q-126353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "c01515fc00562e5e50184150fe5e9cf36bab5bc527378c28178084c47e6ee94b"} {"question" "q-126353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "D=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "E=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "c01515fc00562e5e50184150fe5e9cf36bab5bc527378c28178084c47e6ee94b"} {"question" "q-126353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "c01515fc00562e5e50184150fe5e9cf36bab5bc527378c28178084c47e6ee94b"} {"question" "q-68740" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040926/state.json" "file_sha256" "c01515fc00562e5e50184150fe5e9cf36bab5bc527378c28178084c47e6ee94b"} {"question" "q-68740" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $C$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $B$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear